# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MKJ StudyOS — build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) only if you want cloud accounts.
# An APK built without these runs entirely on the device and needs no backend.
#
# NEVER put a Supabase service-role key, a database password or an AI provider
# key in here: everything in this file is compiled into the APK and readable by
# anyone who unpacks it. Only the *anon* key is safe, and only because
# row-level security is enabled on every table.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase anon (public) key
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional: mark a build as production (used in diagnostics only)
# VITE_APP_ENV=production

# Demo fixtures. Leave this unset for anything a student installs: unset means
# "on in `vite dev`, off in `vite build`". Only the Playwright suite sets it to
# true so its tests have sample data.
# VITE_DEMO_FIXTURES=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never prefix these with VITE_, they would ship in the APK.
# Set them with `supabase secrets set` (see docs/BACKEND_SETUP.md).
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=...                 (provided automatically by Supabase)
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...            (provided automatically by Supabase)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...    (provided automatically by Supabase)
#   AI_PROVIDER=gemini|openai
#   AI_API_KEY=...
#   AI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash (or gpt-4o-mini, etc.)
#   AI_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
#   AI_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_HOUR=20
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
